  "notes": "Sprint 148 Scope Sanitizer false positive fix implemented:\n\n1. scope-sanitizer.ts: Added 3 new filter rules:\n   - Rule 9: isJsAccessPattern() — rejects .directories, .some, .filter etc. (with KNOWN_DOTFILES whitelist for .gitignore, .npmrc etc.)\n   - Rule 10: isPlaceholderPath() — rejects foo.ts, bar.js, example.ts, test.ts (exact base-name match only, composite names like foo-bar.ts preserved)\n   - Both functions exported for testing\n\n2. task-builder.ts: Added maskCodeBlocks() helper:\n   - Fenced code blocks (```...```) are masked before scope extraction in both parseStructuredDirectives() and parseBulletOrNumberedTasks()\n   - Uses parallel masked/original line arrays — masked lines for path detection, original lines for actual extraction\n   - Preserves line count for alignment\n\n3. tests/orchestra/scope-sanitizer-v2.test.ts: 12 tests (all pass):\n   - Placeholder path rejection, JS access pattern rejection, code block masking, Sprint 148 T-002 replay, edge cases\n\n4. tests/orchestra/task-builder.test.ts: Updated 1 existing test that used placeholder filenames (foo.ts, bar.ts → config.ts, types.ts)\n\ntsc --noEmit: 0 errors in modified files (2 pre-existing errors in src/connectors/discord.ts from another task)\nAll 247 related tests pass (10 existing sanitizer + 12 new v2 + 225 task-builder)",
